      "writtenOn": "2020-05-29T16:57:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this is creating a relationship between config options in which TCPC-driven FRS is the default, and PPC-driven FRS is subordinate. I think it would make more sense to have a method-agnostic CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS (or similar), which would be set automatically based on CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_TCPC or CONFIG_USB_PD_FRS_PPC, which would be what a board file would set. If possible, the code in the PE (or wherever) that enables or disables FRS would be method-agnostic. This might benefit from something like pd_frs_enable (or similar) in usb_common.c, somewhat analogous to pd_check_vbus_level.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 639,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 640,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "7b432baf345f1dddc7278ab4331e425ba1ee6c4c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
