      "writtenOn": "2020-05-30T16:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like this direction.  I can also see where it is not exclusive as to TCPC or PPC.  Zork uses the board_tcpc_fast_role_swap_enable to adjust the GPIOs for the PPC. Making this change would allow me to hook my PPC driver and we could off the board_tcpc_fast_role_swap_enable.  The decision to call one of the functions could be based on drv-\u003eset_frs_enable being present in the respective tcpc/ppc structures.  At that point, I am not sure I see a need for the CONFIG_USB_PD_FAST_ROLE_SWAP_PPC.",
